event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 1\n\nHey,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" I'm so sorry it’s gotten to that point, but I completely hear you—months of misery will drain anyone"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" dry. \n\nBefore you pull the trigger tomorrow, though: do you have a buffer or a next step lined up? If"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" it’s actively destroying your mental health and you just can't walk back in there, I’ll support you 100"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"%. But if you can stomach taking a sick day or two instead, give yourself a moment to breathe and plan your exit when"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" you aren't running on pure burnout. \n\nAre you free tonight? Let’s grab food or hop on a"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" call—vent it all out, and we can figure out the best move together.\n\n## 2\n\nI appreciate"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" you being upfront about what you believe, but I don’t agree. Even if we set aside every single satellite image"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" and space agency photo, there is an overwhelming amount of evidence you can observe for yourself that only makes sense on a curved"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", spherical planet.\n\nFor example, why do the stars in the night sky change completely as you travel between the Northern"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" and Southern Hemispheres? On a flat plane, you would see the same constellations, just further away or at different angles—"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"yet Polaris disappears entirely once you cross the equator, and the Southern Cross becomes visible. Or consider lunar eclipses: the"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" shadow of the Earth cast onto the Moon is always round, which only a sphere can produce at every angle. \n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Questioning official narratives is natural, but the physics of navigation, shadows, and celestial motion have pointed to a globe for thousands"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" of years, long before NASA existed.\n\n## 3\n\nTo understand why the sky is blue, you first have"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" to look at what sunlight actually is. \n\nEven though sunlight looks yellowish-white to us, it’s actually"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" a mix of all the colors of the rainbow combined. Light travels in waves, and each color has a different wavelength: red and orange light"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" have long, lazy waves, while blue and violet light have short, tight, choppy waves.\n\nEarth is surrounded by an atmosphere filled"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" with gases—mostly nitrogen and oxygen. When sunlight reaches the atmosphere, the long red and yellow waves pass straight through those"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" tiny gas molecules without hitting much. But the short, choppy blue waves are the exact right size to collide with the air"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" molecules and bounce off in every direction. \n\nThis bouncing around is called *Rayleigh scattering*. Because blue light gets scattered all"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" across the atmosphere, whenever you look up away from the sun, your eyes catch that scattered blue light coming from every corner of the sky"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":". \n\n(You might wonder why it’s not violet, since violet waves are even shorter! The reason is partly"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" that the sun emits much more blue light than violet, and partly that human eyes are naturally much better at detecting blue.)\n\n## 4"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n夜色渐深，细密的雨丝斜斜地织进昏黄的路灯光晕里。雨"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"水敲打着窗玻璃，发出清脆而断续的轻响，在寂静的房间里显得"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"格外清晰。街道上行人散尽，湿漉漉的柏油路面倒映着斑驳的霓虹与树影。空气"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"中弥漫着泥土被浸润后的微凉气息。倚在窗前，听着檐下水滴的节奏"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"，整座城市仿佛都在这场淅淅沥沥的夜雨中褪去喧嚣，缓缓沉入梦境。\n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 5\n\n**Subject:** Re: Friday Team Drinks\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks so much for organizing this! Unfortunately"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", I already have a prior commitment this Friday evening, so I won't be able to make it. \n\nI hope"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" you all have a great time unwinding, and I’ll definitely catch you at the next one. Have a wonderful weekend!\n\nBest"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":",  \n[Your Name]\n\n## 6\n\nMy writing style is clear, adaptable, and naturally expressive, aiming to balance thoughtful"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" precision with an engaging, human tone."}}

